cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >
  If you use this software in your research, please cite it using
  the following metadata. Fill in the fields marked [REQUIRED] before
  publishing. Do not cite placeholder values.

title: "VAE Project: Variational Autoencoder Study for MNIST and Fashion-MNIST"
type: software
version: "0.1.0"

# [REQUIRED] Replace with actual author information
authors:
  - family-names: "[AUTHOR_LAST_NAME]"
    given-names: "[AUTHOR_FIRST_NAME]"
    affiliation: "[INSTITUTION]"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/[YOUR-ORCID-ID]"  # Optional

# [REQUIRED] Replace with actual publication date
date-released: "2024-01-01"

repository-code: "https://github.com/joaopaulo164/vae-project"

abstract: >
  A complete, reproducible Python project for training and analyzing
  Variational Autoencoders (VAEs) on MNIST and Fashion-MNIST datasets.
  Includes latent space analysis with PCA, UMAP, and t-SNE projections,
  systematic topology selection, latent dimension comparison, and an
  optional supervised classification extension. Designed for scientific
  reproducibility and evidence generation for academic publications.

keywords:
  - variational autoencoder
  - VAE
  - latent space
  - MNIST
  - Fashion-MNIST
  - dimensionality reduction
  - deep learning
  - PyTorch
  - reproducible research

license: MIT

